<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom losing Lufthansa business-report.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom losing Lufthansa business-report.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German phone giant Deutsche Telekom AG was losing national airline Lufthansa AG as a customer to the start-up network led by diversified utility Viag AG, the newsweekly Focus said on Sunday.</p>
<p>In June several Lufthansa locations began using telecommunications services from Viag Interkom GmbH and would completely switch over from Telekom by the end of 1998, Focus said in an advance copy of an article due to appear on Monday.</p>
<p>Viag Interkom, a venture with British Telecommunicaitnos Plc, signed a prliminary interconnection agreement with Telekom last month, enabling it to gain access to customers via Telekom's network.</p>
<p>The Lufthansa business was worth tens of millions of marks, Focus said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
